# Day 30

**44km / 11.5 hours**

Wow that was a long day. I wanted to do one to see what it would be like on my body and I guess I'll get the answer. Also I tend to want to just power through boring sections and the current one certainly is dull with the road walking ad nauseum.

Yay road walking! Some of the roads early on were ridiculously high quality given how small the areas are and how far away we are from Auckland at this point. The sprawl continues I suppose.

![Building more houses even further from Auckland because there's not enough traffic](./construction.jpg)

The road walking continues for a while before finally coming to a track although it's a grassy open walk up a hill which is pleasant enough. From the hill there's some solid views of the area. 

![One of the views from the hill top. I wasn't overwhelmed or anything but it was okay.](./hill-view.jpg)

After coming down the other side of the hill there was a short section of some wonderful flora i.e. plants that felt actually enjoyable to walk through before leaving that for more roads. At this point there was a place I could stop after around 30km for the day but I decided to power through and get the next set of roads done with. 

To describe the roads for walking on feels like describing the taste of rocks: it's not what they're designed for so it's never going to be pleasant although some might be less unpleasant than others. There was a stretch of state highway which was particularly concerning especially when the road narrowed over a bridge. There was also a farm road which was not nice when large machinery drove over it sending dust everywhere. 

![Some of the many cows inhabiting the farm](./farm-cows.jpg)

The farm road led to a small river crossing and some grassy walking along the riverbank. At this point I was really struggling as my legs hurt, my feet hurt and my shoulders hurt. I was running on the sugary treats I had brought with me and was consuming at a rapid rate. There was still more than 5km to go but I had to struggle onwards. 

![The route sneaking under the bridge to continue near the road](./bridge-underpass.jpg)

Finally after the longest day so far, certainly in terms of distance I made it to the town where I could stay. I think I'll have to check how my body feels tomorrow before doing more days like this one. It does make the logistics nicer if I can do longer days but it's tough on the body and I'm not really in a rush.